# swingbus rules

Read `AGENTS.md` for full context (flows, architecture, stops, open items). These rules are non-negotiable:

## Naming and copy
- The product name is **swingbus**, always lowercase — including at the start of a sentence, titles, metadata, and docs. Never "Swingbus" or "Swing Bus".
- Keep the footer on every page (in `src/app/layout.tsx`):
  - "swingbus brought to you by your friends in Transportation and Observability Software."
  - "Feedback? Find us at #memphis-transportation on Slack."
- Minimize text. No explanatory paragraphs on selection screens; prefer short labels, icons, and one clear action.

## Visual design (Uber-like)
- Dark by default on every device, whatever the system setting: black background, white text, white primary buttons, gray (`--mist`, #262626) inputs, list rows with hairline dividers. Light is the same inverted (white background, black text and buttons, #EEE inputs).
- The sun/moon switch (`ThemeToggle`) stays in every page header (`AppHeader`, plus the home header); each device remembers its pick (`localStorage` `swingbus.theme`). The inline `<head>` script in `src/app/layout.tsx` (`THEME_BOOT_SCRIPT`, `src/lib/theme.ts`) applies it before first paint: never move it into an effect, and don't add `themeColor` to the Next viewport (the script owns the `theme-color` meta).
- Colors come only from the tokens in `globals.css` (`bg-foam`, `text-ink-soft`, `bg-strong`/`text-on-strong`, `bg-raised`, `sb-night`, `text-on-volt`…), never `bg-white`, `bg-black` or hex. Every pair meets WCAG AA in both schemes; `npm test` checks them (`src/lib/theme.test.ts`), so add new pairs there.
- One accent: electric yellow `--volt` (#FFD400). Use it as a fill (bolt logo, live dot, "at stop" chip, highlights on black), with black text on it. Never yellow text on white.
- Logo is the yellow lightning bolt on a black rounded square (`src/components/brand.tsx`, `public/bolt.svg`); on dark pages it and the shuttle chips get a hairline ring.
- Paper is always light: the dark palette is screen-only, and QR cards are `sb-light` so they print and preview dark modules on white.
- Mobile first: inputs stay 16px, tap targets ≥ 44px, prefer tappable lists over dropdowns for destinations.
- Reuse the `sb-*` classes and components (`AppHeader`, `MiniMap`, icons) instead of new one-off styles.

## Engineering
- Keep custom CSS inside `@layer base` / `@layer components` in `globals.css`; unlayered rules override Tailwind utilities and have hidden button labels before.
- Fonts are bundled with `@fontsource-variable/*`. Do not use `next/font/google` (boot-time downloads fail on restricted networks and take the app down).
- No database: state is `store.json` in `DATA_DIR` (default `data/`, `/data` in the container) via `src/lib/store.ts`; write it only through `persist()` (atomic temp file + rename). One file behind an in-process lock means exactly one process: no horizontal scaling, no serverless. Bump `SCHEMA_VERSION` and add a migration when the shape changes; admin-edited stops must survive restarts and migrations.
- Driver, ground control, and admin are password-gated in `src/middleware.ts` + `src/lib/auth.ts`. Any new driver/admin page or mutating API must be added to `requiredRole`. Passenger pages and `GET /api/health` stay public; anonymous `GET /api/state` returns only the passenger feed (`publicState` in `src/lib/feed.ts`), so never add other riders' requests, rider free text, cancel tokens or offline shuttles to it. Production builds must keep refusing to start without real `DRIVER_PASSWORD`, `ADMIN_PASSWORD`, `AUTH_SECRET` (`authConfigProblem()`); never add production fallbacks.
- Never commit real passwords or tokens; use `DRIVER_PASSWORD`, `ADMIN_PASSWORD`, `AUTH_SECRET` env vars.
- Dev server: `npm run dev` on port 43127 (`scripts/dev-forever.sh` auto-restarts). Run `npx tsc --noEmit`, `npx eslint src`, and `npm test` before committing.
